<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Keyonte George on a Rookie Contract?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>George is paid <strong>$6.56m</strong> because the rookie scale fixes the number by draft position, and the 16th pick is paid what the 16th pick is paid.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went 16th in 2023 out of Baylor after one season.</li>
<li>All four years are worth <strong>$18.82m</strong>, fully guaranteed.</li>
<li>Utah exercised both options ahead of their deadlines.</li>
<li>The final year is the largest, at <strong>$6.56m</strong>.</li>
<li>His five-year extension, worth up to <strong>$157.5m</strong>, starts next season.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has never been paid by another club.</p>

